# NEW UPDATES: Auth Fix, Emails & Database Integration

## 4. Authentication Bug Fix
You encountered an issue where user registration wasn't working.
* **The fix**: The frontend registration page was sending the variable `phoneNumber` in its API payload, but the backend [User.js](file:///d:/crowdsource_lost_and_found/backend/models/User.js) database exclusively expected the variable to be named `phone`. I corrected the variable mapping, so Registration and Login now work flawlessly on the frontend!

## 5. Connecting Items to the Backend Database
The biggest missing link was that reported items were not being securely stored.
* **API Integration**: [ReportFoundItem.jsx](file:///d:/crowdsource_lost_and_found/fwd_project/src/components/ReportFoundItem.jsx) and [ReportLostItem.jsx](file:///d:/crowdsource_lost_and_found/fwd_project/src/components/ReportLostItem.jsx) have been upgraded to send a secure `POST` request to your backend server. Whenever you report an item, it uses your encrypted token to securely pin the item directly to your `userId` and Email natively in MongoDB!
* **Fetching Items**: [ThingsFoundPage](file:///d:/crowdsource_lost_and_found/fwd_project/src/components/ThingsFoundPage.jsx#6-176) has been rewritten. Instead of using a buggy, temporary local array, it now securely fetches all items over the network using your backend `GET` routes. This means items survive page reloads and are universally accessible by all signed-in users!

## 6. Email Notifications 
* **Nodemailer Setup**: Because Items are now securely tied to a User's account in the backend, the Messaging controller can intelligently look up who originally found the item! Every time a user sends a message through the modal, the backend automatically extracts the finder's exact registered email address and sends an email notification. 

> [!TIP]
> **To Test Emailing right now:**
> Ensure you reload both your Terminal (`npm run dev`) and React (`npm run dev`). Because there are no real credentials in your [.env](file:///d:/crowdsource_lost_and_found/backend/.env) right now, when you test sending a message to a Founder, Node will securely generate a mock *Test Email*. 
> Immediately look at your Backend Terminal, and you will see a `---- PREVIEW EMAIL URL: https://... ----`. Clik that URL to instantly see a preview of the Email that the Founder would successfully receive!


## How to Test Everything
1. Make sure MongoDB and your `backend` server are running.
2. Log into Account A and go to **Report Found**. Post a new item!
3. Open an Incognito window, and log into Account B.
4. From Account B, go to **Things Found**, find Account A's item, and click "Message Finder".
5. Send a message. You will see it appear in real-time, and a Test Email Preview URL will be generated in your backend Terminal, proving the message flawlessly routed to Account A's profile!
